      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(crestodian): run approval-intent classifier on the utilityModel, not flagship (#102360)",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe Crestodian approval-intent classifier (`classifyCrestodianApprovalIntent`, `src/crestodian/approval-intent.ts`) resolves the completion model **without** `useUtilityModel: true`, so an ambiguous approval reply that reaches the model path runs on the agent's **flagship** model to decide a single approve/decline/other label. It was the only member of the simple-completion family (e.g. `conversation-label-generator.ts`) that omitted the flag, so every ambiguous approval reply is billed at flagship pricing for a fixed ~8-token structured answer. Fixes #102360.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nA one-word bounded classification is exactly the \"utility work\" the rest of the family already runs on the configured `utilityModel`. `prepareSimpleCompletionModelForAgent` already supports `useUtilityModel` (resolves `agents.defaults.utilityModel`); the classifier just wasn't passing it. Adding `useUtilityModel: true` aligns it with the family and the cheaper tier.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators who configure a distinct `utilityModel` (the intended cheap tier for bounded classification) stop paying flagship pricing for ambiguous approval-flow replies. No behavior change to the classification result — only the model tier that judges it.\n\n## Evidence\n\nReal `classifyCrestodianApprovalIntent` call with an ambiguous message (model path), capturing what model prep receives:\n```\nbefore (main):    prepare called with useUtilityModel = undefined   ← flagship\nafter  (this PR): prepare called with useUtilityModel = true        ← utilityModel\n```\nAdded a regression test asserting `prepareSimpleCompletionModelForAgent` is called with `{ useUtilityModel: true }`. `tsgo:core` 0 errors; `approval-intent.test.ts` green (8 tests: 7 existing + 1 new).\n",
        "branch": "fix/crestodian-approval-intent-utility-model-102360",
